# Independent compact-criterion scope review

**Status:** Read-only review; proposed contract and implementation remain unimplemented.
**Reviewed:** Revision-2 `contract.md` and `implementation-design.md`, current doctrine, and exact arithmetic on 2026-10-16 UTC.

The revision-2 limited claim is defensible for the user's chosen compact recipes
and unchanged per-run budgets. It supplies an independently specified procedure;
it does not retroactively supply independent origins for historical floors or
establish published-model parity. Root has accepted this limited claim subject
to the concrete boundary clarifications below. No phase is closed by this review.

## Exact approved claim

For each canonical supervised row and real lane, execute all five prescribed
training seeds `canonicalBase + [0..4]`, in order and at the unchanged budget.
Keep index 0 as the predetermined serving run. Preserve all finite outcomes,
including below-floor, below-signal and non-improving runs. Missing, incomplete,
non-finite, substituted, duplicated or wrong-budget children fail qualification;
none may be replaced or omitted from the five-run median.

At least three children must **jointly** improve their own exact initial held-out
score and pass the defined constant/uniform-reference or best-constant regression
control. The median over all five final primary metrics must clear the exact
unchanged historical floor. Index 0 must independently pass the floor, signal,
improvement, real execution, completion and admitted-artifact checks. Its own
served metric stays the checkpoint's metric; cohort median/N remain separately
typed and authenticated. A passing cohort cannot borrow another seed's weights
or publish a failing index 0.

This is observed predictive improvement on the pinned benchmark, supported by
five actual training runs and authentic artifacts. It is not population
generalization, application utility, generic feature dependence, or evidence that
the original published architecture/schedule was reproduced. Existing real
device, curve-sanity, split, determinism and standing-gate requirements continue.

## Independent arithmetic and probability scope

I independently summed the exact binomial integer weights and verified both
sides of each critical boundary at `n=1000`, alpha `1/5000`:

| Semantic classes | First passing count | Previous count fails |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| 10 | 136 | 135 |
| 100 | 24 | 23 |
| 200 | 16 | 15 |

The actual classifier requirement is `max(majorityCount+1, criticalCount)`.
Semantic class count comes from the canonical projection, not observed-label
coverage or outputs. The exact results/input hashes are retained in
`independent-arithmetic-and-inputs.json`. Classification ties and regression
exact-SSE ties fail improvement. Exact finite binary64 rational SSE comparisons
cannot borrow a parity epsilon; non-finite initialization must not be treated as
infinite loss. Regression's strictly positive empirical R² is descriptive and
receives no probability claim.

Let `J_s` be joint success and `N=sum J_s`. Under a cohort's **all-five** null,
each seed's predicted labels are independent uniform draws over the held-out
examples, independent of those labels. Each `J_s` is a subset of that seed's
binomial-tail event, so `E[N] <= 5/5000`. The pointwise inequality
`3 * 1{N>=3} <= N` gives `P(N>=3) <= 1/3000`. The union bound over at most thirty
classification row/lane cohorts is at most `0.01`. I also checked the pointwise
inequality for every one of the 32 binary joint-success patterns. Cross-seed and
cross-cohort independence is unnecessary.

The mandatory index-0 joint success and historical median restriction only make
the complete ProductRow passing event smaller. The stated conservative bound is
therefore valid; it need not be tightened to justify the chosen alpha.

This bound does **not** cover a mixed cohort containing some skilled predictors,
nor prove that three members have population signal. More generally, random
neural-network initialization shares weights across examples and need not obey
the iid uniform-per-example null. Do not turn this hypothetical reference bound
into “a probability of false learning below 1%” for arbitrary untrained or
feature-independent algorithms. Majority rejects every fixed constant on these
labels; it does not turn the uniform null into all input-independent predictors.
The [NIST binomial definition](https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/eda/section3/eda366i.htm)
and [union inequality](https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/prc/section4/prc473.htm)
support the stated reference calculations, not those broader claims.

Keep an append-only attempt ledger and the fixed first family of at most thirty
qualifying classification cohorts. A score-selected retry or newly chosen seed
pool does not receive the same error budget for free. A later correction needs
an explicitly disclosed additional family/budget or a narrower probability
claim. Existing public, previously examined benchmarks do not become fresh
population samples after versioning; [Cawley and Talbot](https://www.jmlr.org/papers/v11/cawley10a.html)
support the selection-bias limitation. These statements preserve the intended
finite-benchmark scope without inventing confidence for regression/improvement.

## Required doctrine reconciliation

Current `DEVELOPMENT_PLAN/README.md:4127` requires literature-derived statistical
convergence and `:4296` describes frozen external constants; current
`README.md:2553` and `:2602` prescribe five-training-seed target-minus-slack
convergence. `product_completion_contract.md:83` also calls the bar externally
anchored. The new finite compact qualification is an overt prospective
reconciliation of those words, not an implementation that already satisfies
them unchanged.

Freeze **the constants and comparison procedures**, independently of the final
measurement. Authentic pre-update initial weights, data-only majority counts
and target variance supply separate comparison inputs. They are not themselves
all literal external constants. Do not characterize this necessary clarification
as proof that a measured-derived historical floor was always external. Tiny's
`0.008` and other unproven/project-calibrated floors remain unchanged additional
restrictions with their true provenance. Their conjunction with the new rule
cannot repair that origin. Source comments, engineering contracts and current
UI/report labels need the same distinction, even if legacy field names remain.

This review approves the **SL** proposal. It does not independently justify
unrelated RL slack, declare all Exit-26 surfaces satisfied, or waive another
owned obligation. Exact original loss/gradient curve sanity, real device
execution, deterministic replay and independent train/selection/final-test
membership remain required. Phase 278 owns actual qualification evidence before
closure; Phase 285 may consume the mechanism/artifact later but is not an
implementation or evidence prerequisite. The current local-gate ownership
proposal and Phase 279 behavioral detector remain separate and unimplemented.

## Concrete implementation boundary corrections

Revision 2 has incorporated the first four clarifications; preserve them in code:

1. Put the primitive `SupervisedSeedIndex` and seed-pool/policy data in a lower
   pure module. A cohort module may import Matrix; Matrix cannot import that
   module for its index type and create a dependency cycle.
2. Static descriptor equality excludes **only parameter payload values**. Bind
   shape, operator geometry, activation/mode, parameter tensor layout/order,
   transforms and all nonparameter inference state. Capture actual initial
   parameters before the first optimizer step. Regression must return its real
   `params0`, rather than reinitialize after observing the final run. A future
   nonparameter state needs an explicit captured snapshot policy.
3. Pair replay recomputes predictions and metrics. It verifies authenticated
   producer-observed counters/device evidence and expected-budget algebra; final
   weights alone cannot reconstruct the actual optimizer update history.
4. Preserve all existing curve, split, real-device and determinism obligations;
   do not replace them with one scalar improvement check.
5. Keep raw budget-complete outcomes distinct from `CompletedTraining` and Store
   admission. Use a preliminary verified raw cohort predicate, then index-0
   ordinary completion/write/admission, then a qualification artifact referencing
   that exact admitted checkpoint. The checkpoint need not point back to the
   artifact; a later authenticated report references both. This avoids both hash
   cycles and an eligibility-before-admission type cycle.

The reader must hash/load all referenced snapshots, data/order and weights;
replay the pair under the same bound serving semantics; reconstruct the exact
ordered children; and verify current policy, plan, device/source authority and
the index-0 physical/Store tuple. Caller-created internally consistent JSON is
not authentic training evidence. No untrained or below-floor model receives a
forged completed artifact merely to make the cohort reader convenient.

No source, threshold, seed, budget, plan status, primary container, or native
binary was changed by this review. Pure policy API review, adversarial tests,
real five-run cohorts and fresh owned journals/gates remain subsequent work.
